TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Reproduced the exact failure predicted by overseer steers 9 and 10: checkpoint cp-smoke ran against base revision 6e818349eeb947501ac04ba83e826764a042011c, which does not contain the stdin fix ae10e94, so scripts/run-smoke.sh:10 still invokes `podman run --rm --device /dev/kfd ... python3 -` without `-i`. Verified in the lane worktree: `git merge-base --is-ancestor ae10e94 HEAD` is false (the commit object exists but is not in this lineage), and `grep -n 'podman run' scripts/run-smoke.sh` shows the invocation with no `-i` flag. Consequence: the `<<'PY'` heredoc never reaches the container's stdin, `python3 -` reads EOF and executes nothing, no probe output is produced, results/receipts/smoke.json is never written (results/receipts contains only build.json, weights-coordinator.json, weights-worker.json; results/receipts/failed/ does not exist), and the validator exits 1. The capture at /home/tom/.local/state/tally/capture/archive/01a051db-172f-7b10-ab67-fcf08144418f.cp-smoke/checkpoint.json confirms this shape: empty stderr, exitCode 1, and stdout containing only the wrapper's own \"smoke receipt: ...\" line with no receipt json from the container. This is not a new defect and not a machinery fault: the probe TypeError fix (7509202) and the checkpoint-purity guard (9480958) are both present at 6e81834 and remain correct but unreachable, exactly as steer 9 stated (\"if the next attempt still bases on 6e81834 the heredoc still won't arrive — that failure would be expected, not new\"). The cause lies wholly outside cp-smoke's authorized paths — cp-smoke is a checkpoint task whose command is fixed by the worklist and which must not modify the repository, so no in-task edit could add `-i`. The required action is integration-lineage, not implementation: the checkpoint must be re-run on a base whose ancestry includes ae10e94. Steer 10 reports the campaign was re-armed (arm 6) to found on ae10e94, but this attempt's workspace baseRev and head were both 6e81834, so the re-arm had not reached this lane. No proposal is included because the source fix already exists on main and no worklist amendment or authority grant would change the outcome; what is needed is for the arm-6 lineage carrying ae10e94 to become this checkpoint's base before cp-smoke is dispatched again. Expected result once it does: the container executes the probe program with the 7509202 boolean-predicate admission fix, all five probes (arch, fp8_cast, registry, aperture, admission) report, results/receipts/smoke.json lands with status pass, and the validator exits 0."}
